# Email transport providers

Transactional and marketing email go through a **provider registry**. The
**built-in default** is Nodemailer (SMTP), configured via `bermooda.config.js`.
Optional ESP transports ship as external plugins (`@bermooda/plugin-resend`,
`@bermooda/plugin-sendgrid`, `@bermooda/plugin-aws-ses`). Only one email
provider plugin can be active at a time — activate it under **Admin → Plugins**;
that replaces Nodemailer as the active transport until the plugin is disabled.

Relevant modules: [app/libs/email/index.server.js](mdc:app/libs/email/index.server.js),
[app/libs/email/nodemailer.server.js](mdc:app/libs/email/nodemailer.server.js),
[app/libs/email-types.server.js](mdc:app/libs/email-types.server.js), plugin
sources in sibling repos (`../plugin-resend`, `../plugin-sendgrid`,
`../plugin-aws-ses`), templates in [app/emails/index.server.jsx](mdc:app/emails/index.server.jsx).

## What to call

| Use case | Import | Notes |
| ----- | --- | ----- |
| Send a named template | `sendWelcomeEmail`, `sendOrderConfirmationEmail`, … from `#/emails/index.server` | Renders React Email → HTML, then active provider |
| Raw HTML send | `sendEmail` from `#/libs/email/index.server` | Low-level; uses Nodemailer unless an email plugin is active |
| Custom / plugin provider | `defineProvider('email', { name, send })` | Enable under Admin → Plugins (exclusive with other email plugins) |

Do **not** import ESP SDKs from app code outside email provider plugins.
Nodemailer is the sole built-in transport SDK allowed under `#/libs/email`.

## Configuration

From [bermooda.config.example.js](mdc:bermooda.config.example.js):

- `email.fromNoReply` — sender used for transactional and auth mail
- `email.smtp` — optional Nodemailer transport options (object or connection URL). When omitted, Nodemailer defaults to `localhost:587` with no auth (Mailpit/MailHog/local MTA).

From [`.env.example`](mdc:.env.example):

- `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` — also used to encrypt plugin password settings at rest

Activate an optional ESP plugin in **Admin → Plugins → Email providers** and
enter API keys in that plugin's settings form (encrypted in the `Setting`
table). Install with `bermooda plugin add` when needed — default
`npm run setup` / `bermooda install` do not enable one.

## Custom providers (plugins)

```js
import { definePlugin, defineProvider } from '#/core/plugins/index.server';

export const pluginManifest = definePlugin({
  providers: {
    postmark: defineProvider('email', {
      name: 'Postmark',
      async send({ from, to, subject, html, text }) {
        return { success: true };
      },
    }),
  },
});
```

Enabling your plugin deactivates any other email provider plugin automatically
and becomes the active transport (Nodemailer remains registered as fallback).
